00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:06,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:07,112 --> 00:00:11,033
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:46,694 --> 00:00:48,612
A LOVE OTHER THAN YOURS

3
00:00:48,737 --> 00:00:50,239
[theme music concludes]

4
00:00:52,658 --> 00:00:53,492
ALL PERSONS, LOCATIONS, RELIGIONS,
INCIDENTS, AND ORGANIZATIONS IN THIS DRAMA

5
00:00:53,617 --> 00:00:54,451
ARE FICTITIOUS

6
00:00:54,577 --> 00:00:55,411
CHILD ACTORS HAVE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER PARENTAL SUPERVISION

7
00:00:55,536 --> 00:00:56,370
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

8
00:00:58,163 --> 00:01:01,709
-Marry me, Mi-do.
-[sentimental instrumental music playing]

9
00:01:04,712 --> 00:01:07,756
Please, let's get… married.

10
00:01:10,217 --> 00:01:11,176
[hiccups]

11
00:01:14,930 --> 00:01:16,015
[hiccups]

12
00:01:22,146 --> 00:01:28,027
3. CAN WE FEEL THAT SPARK AGAIN?

13
00:01:34,033 --> 00:01:35,784
[Mi-do]  The thought suddenly hit me.

14
00:01:37,369 --> 00:01:39,163
If I broke up with Namgung,

15
00:01:39,288 --> 00:01:41,957
how many books
would no longer be part of my life?

16
00:01:43,876 --> 00:01:47,212
Could I really live
after losing all those dear books?

17
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:50,674
[sighs]

18
00:01:53,218 --> 00:01:54,178
[sighs]

19
00:01:54,929 --> 00:01:55,846
No.

20
00:01:55,971 --> 00:01:57,348
[sighs deeply]

21
00:01:57,473 --> 00:02:00,434
Could I really go on
living without Namgung?

22
00:02:08,150 --> 00:02:09,234
[sighs]

23
00:02:11,946 --> 00:02:15,157
[sentimental instrumental music continues]

24
00:02:15,282 --> 00:02:17,618
[panting softly]

25
00:02:30,923 --> 00:02:31,966
[sighs]

26
00:02:34,301 --> 00:02:39,098
[pants]

27
00:02:49,483 --> 00:02:50,943
[Suk-hee]  His name is Namgung.

28
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:55,406
Actually, he's the same age as Mi-do…

29
00:02:55,531 --> 00:02:56,407
THE SORROWS OF YOUNG WERTHER

30
00:02:56,532 --> 00:02:59,159
…and he'll be living with us
starting today.

31
00:03:00,494 --> 00:03:03,163
Sweetie, you should say hello too.

32
00:03:05,290 --> 00:03:08,043
What is it? Are you feeling shy?

33
00:03:08,585 --> 00:03:09,628
[chuckles softly]

34
00:03:21,890 --> 00:03:23,017
[inhales softly]

35
00:03:26,061 --> 00:03:28,022
[music softens]

36
00:03:30,941 --> 00:03:33,360
[music rises]

37
00:03:38,490 --> 00:03:42,786
[mixer whirring]

38
00:03:53,005 --> 00:03:54,757
[oven fire crackling]

39
00:03:56,842 --> 00:03:58,218
Ah, it's hot! Hot, hot!

40
00:04:01,388 --> 00:04:03,807
[Sang-hun] Excuse me, sir.
What are you doing?

41
00:04:03,932 --> 00:04:05,559
-[Namgung] Hey, come taste this.
-Huh?

42
00:04:06,518 --> 00:04:09,813
-[music concludes]
-[blows air, munches]

43
00:04:09,938 --> 00:04:12,816
-[chewing] It's hot.
-[gasping, grunting]

44
00:04:12,941 --> 00:04:14,568
[munches] Mm, mm.

45
00:04:14,693 --> 00:04:16,570
What… What is this? I know this taste.

46
00:04:18,155 --> 00:04:19,740
Corn Stick. Am I right?

47
00:04:19,865 --> 00:04:22,367
They're discontinued.
Why are you making this?

48
00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:27,206
[pan sizzling]

49
00:04:27,331 --> 00:04:29,249
You all right? [exhales]

50
00:04:33,170 --> 00:04:34,296
Hmm. [sniffs]

51
00:04:35,881 --> 00:04:36,965
[pan sizzling]

52
00:04:37,216 --> 00:04:40,761
Ah, jeez. Is she skipping again?

53
00:04:41,512 --> 00:04:44,723
This is her father's memorial
and she decides to skip out?

54
00:04:46,809 --> 00:04:50,854
Can you just dry that base already?
It's still completely wet, man.

55
00:04:52,689 --> 00:04:53,857
I'm already doing it.

56
00:04:54,608 --> 00:04:57,528
[pan sizzling]

57
00:04:58,112 --> 00:04:59,238
[match strikes]

58
00:05:06,161 --> 00:05:07,162
[Yeong-do blows air]

59
00:05:08,664 --> 00:05:09,665
[grunts softly]

60
00:05:09,790 --> 00:05:11,708
-[door opens]
-[bells jangling]

61
00:05:25,347 --> 00:05:26,265
[Mi-do sighs]

62
00:05:27,057 --> 00:05:28,183
EXORCISM CHRONICLES

63
00:05:44,741 --> 00:05:50,622
-[cutlery clinking]
-[munching]

64
00:05:52,249 --> 00:05:54,585
-Isn't that comic wrong for a memorial?
-[hiccups]

65
00:05:55,669 --> 00:05:57,671
-Water, some water.
-Mm-hmm.

66
00:05:57,796 --> 00:06:00,215
So, this is what Dad used to read, huh?

67
00:06:01,550 --> 00:06:04,011
He used to put me in a stroller
and take me to the bookstore.

68
00:06:04,136 --> 00:06:06,930
-He's making things up again, huh?
-You know it's true.

69
00:06:07,055 --> 00:06:08,640
-I'm not making anything up.
-[both whisper indistinctly]

70
00:06:08,765 --> 00:06:09,766
[Wan-do] I actually remember it.

71
00:06:09,892 --> 00:06:11,476
But he also read
a lot of comic books, right?

72
00:06:11,602 --> 00:06:13,478
[clears throat] So…

73
00:06:13,604 --> 00:06:15,647
-there's something that I--
-[Yeong-do] That's nonsense.

74
00:06:15,772 --> 00:06:18,233
Dad only ever read novels,
fantasy and martial arts.

75
00:06:18,358 --> 00:06:20,944
Wrong, man. I remember it clearly.

76
00:06:21,069 --> 00:06:23,488
-He looked really happy reading them.
-[Yeong-do] That's not true.

77
00:06:23,614 --> 00:06:26,200
His favorite books were  Dark Mage,

78
00:06:26,325 --> 00:06:28,994
-Dragon Raja,  and  Temple of the Dragon.
-[whispers indistinctly]

79
00:06:29,119 --> 00:06:32,748
He was strictly a fantasy guy.
Hey, Mi-do, you remember that, don't you?

80
00:06:32,873 --> 00:06:35,626
-We have something to say. [hiccups]
-No way. I remember Dad

81
00:06:35,751 --> 00:06:38,712
at the bookstore reading comics
while pushing me around in the stroller.

82
00:06:38,837 --> 00:06:41,131
Nah, you remembering
what you want doesn't make it true.

83
00:06:41,256 --> 00:06:43,508
I know I'm right. He read those.
Mom, tell him I'm right.

84
00:06:43,634 --> 00:06:45,219
[Yeong-do]
Dad only read novels, all right?

85
00:06:45,344 --> 00:06:48,013
-So, we're gonna get married.
-[dramatic musical sting]

86
00:06:48,138 --> 00:06:52,100
[quirky piano music playing]

87
00:06:52,226 --> 00:06:53,227
Uh…

88
00:06:55,187 --> 00:06:57,272
[vehicle whizzing past outside]

89
00:06:57,397 --> 00:07:01,902
Uh… now I'm embarrassed with the abrupt…

90
00:07:02,027 --> 00:07:03,570
-[exhales deeply]
-…well, attention.

91
00:07:03,695 --> 00:07:05,822
[chopsticks clinking]

92
00:07:05,948 --> 00:07:11,787
I remember Dad liked reading  Sunday Soul.
[gulps, hiccups]

93
00:07:14,164 --> 00:07:16,458
[music concludes]

94
00:07:16,583 --> 00:07:17,918
Do you guys remember…

95
00:07:19,336 --> 00:07:21,171
when I was about three and a half…

96
00:07:23,257 --> 00:07:25,384
years old, a dog lunged at Mi-do?

97
00:07:25,509 --> 00:07:28,470
[Yeong-do] Namgung,
it's your fault he's like this.

98
00:07:28,595 --> 00:07:30,973
You pushed him off a slide
when he was five.

99
00:07:31,098 --> 00:07:32,975
He's been freaking weird ever since then.

100
00:07:33,892 --> 00:07:37,479
We heard a scream of Mi-do,
and Namgung, he…

101
00:07:38,272 --> 00:07:40,732
he left me with you
and ran straight toward her.

102
00:07:40,857 --> 00:07:43,568
Wow. You should have let that dog get her.

103
00:07:43,694 --> 00:07:44,820
Enough.

104
00:07:46,196 --> 00:07:49,825
[chuckles] I'm joking. It's just a joke.

105
00:07:51,201 --> 00:07:54,871
Anyway, I can still remember
that day so clearly.

106
00:07:55,372 --> 00:07:59,334
The temperature, the smell,
the wind, the light.

107
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:05,882
Also… Namgung's back as he ran to Mi-do.

108
00:08:08,427 --> 00:08:09,594
And I knew right there…

109
00:08:11,680 --> 00:08:13,223
that one day you'd get married.

110
00:08:14,224 --> 00:08:16,935
Just say it already.
Mom told you that, yeah?

111
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:19,104
-[gentle guitar music playing]
-Were you in love with her since then?

112
00:08:19,229 --> 00:08:22,524
What? Dude, I was only like ten.

113
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:24,693
So, you've loved her since you were ten?

114
00:08:25,902 --> 00:08:29,323
So boring. Stop talking nonsense.
Come on, food's ready.

115
00:08:36,079 --> 00:08:37,914
The broth is perfect, right?

116
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:40,459
I was known
as the best  ramyeon  maker in my unit.

117
00:08:49,593 --> 00:08:51,303
[both slurp]

118
00:08:51,428 --> 00:08:52,846
I don't know if it was love.

119
00:08:53,764 --> 00:08:55,932
I just needed to protect her
at all costs, you know?

120
00:08:56,058 --> 00:08:59,269
[both slurping]

121
00:09:01,980 --> 00:09:07,235
At first sight, I thought,
"Whoa, she and I are so alike."

122
00:09:10,072 --> 00:09:11,198
I just knew.

123
00:09:13,533 --> 00:09:15,494
So, you loved her since you were seven?

124
00:09:16,328 --> 00:09:17,954
Uh… just eat.

125
00:09:20,123 --> 00:09:21,291
[Wan-do slurping]

126
00:09:22,250 --> 00:09:24,419
-[music concludes]
-[Yeong-do] What?

127
00:09:24,544 --> 00:09:26,004
What do you mean by that?

128
00:09:27,506 --> 00:09:30,217
Forget the special lecture, okay?
How many times do I have to say it?

129
00:09:31,176 --> 00:09:33,261
I asked you to give me
three days' notice, right?

130
00:09:33,387 --> 00:09:36,807
The lecture was scheduled last minute.
Do you think I really want to go?

131
00:09:36,932 --> 00:09:40,852
Hey, you barely see each other.
Don't you feel a little bad for Sang-su?

132
00:09:40,977 --> 00:09:42,437
[Mun-yeong] Of course I feel bad.

133
00:09:42,562 --> 00:09:44,606
That's why I'm calling you,
although I hate doing it.

134
00:09:45,273 --> 00:09:46,316
I mean, come on.

135
00:09:46,441 --> 00:09:48,485
Why else would I be crazy enough
to call you, huh?

136
00:09:48,735 --> 00:09:53,407
[scoffs] Are you serious? What an honor.
Oh, God, I'm fucking thrilled.

137
00:09:53,532 --> 00:09:57,327
Oh, no. Poor Yeong-do.
His life is so very hard.

138
00:09:57,452 --> 00:10:00,288
Stop playing the victim.
You're almost 50 years old. That's low.

139
00:10:00,414 --> 00:10:03,083
The victim, really?
Hey, you're a nuisance.

140
00:10:03,208 --> 00:10:05,252
What? The pity party is over.

141
00:10:05,377 --> 00:10:08,338
Pity party? The fucking audacity.

142
00:10:08,839 --> 00:10:09,756
Every single problem I have…

143
00:10:09,881 --> 00:10:12,092
Good thing we didn't bring Sang-su, right?

144
00:10:12,217 --> 00:10:13,343
[Yeong-do] You've got some fucking nerve…

145
00:10:13,468 --> 00:10:15,262
They wouldn't be fighting if he were here.

146
00:10:15,387 --> 00:10:16,513
[Yeong-do] I'm fine. You calm down.

147
00:10:16,638 --> 00:10:17,472
You think so?

148
00:10:17,597 --> 00:10:19,516
[Yeong-do] Think about our son,
not yourself.

149
00:10:19,641 --> 00:10:21,685
-I'm fishing. How is that a problem?
-Hmm.

150
00:10:23,854 --> 00:10:25,021
How deep are we talking?

151
00:10:25,147 --> 00:10:27,858
[Yeong-do] Forget it. Whatever.
Yeah, yeah, yeah. It's fine.

152
00:10:27,983 --> 00:10:30,318
-I don't need it… [continues indistinctly]
-How about…

153
00:10:32,487 --> 00:10:34,072
-360 feet?
-[Yeong-do] Why'd you call me

154
00:10:34,197 --> 00:10:35,574
-if you're just gonna do…
-That's deep indeed.

155
00:10:35,699 --> 00:10:36,950
…whatever the hell you want.

156
00:10:37,075 --> 00:10:39,619
-Jeez. God.
-[chuckles softly]

157
00:10:39,744 --> 00:10:41,413
[Yeong-do]
I can't stand hearing your voice.

158
00:10:47,377 --> 00:10:48,211
[Mi-do]  Mom…

159
00:10:48,336 --> 00:10:49,796
QUEENS HAIR SALON

160
00:10:49,921 --> 00:10:54,009
…what if I… what if I die
before Namgung does?

161
00:10:54,676 --> 00:10:56,720
[groans, sighs]

162
00:10:56,845 --> 00:10:59,014
Okay, did you really need to do that?

163
00:10:59,139 --> 00:11:02,684
Why are you trying to jinx it?
And right before your wedding?

164
00:11:02,809 --> 00:11:04,895
-Knock wood!
-Knock, knock! Okay.

165
00:11:05,687 --> 00:11:06,855
As I was telling you…

166
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:10,609
you never know
what the future holds, right?

167
00:11:12,652 --> 00:11:14,988
You didn't know Dad
would die so young either.

168
00:11:16,198 --> 00:11:20,827
Anyway, if I die
and Namgung outlives me…

169
00:11:22,537 --> 00:11:25,248
I want him to have
this place after I'm gone.

170
00:11:27,083 --> 00:11:28,126
It's my inheritance.

171
00:11:28,251 --> 00:11:30,295
If I die and you don't give it to him,
I'll come back for you.

172
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:33,423
-Hey!
-[gasps] Why are you raising your voice?

173
00:11:33,548 --> 00:11:34,799
I don't care what you want.

174
00:11:34,925 --> 00:11:38,428
Hoya is getting the whole thing,
so don't get your hopes up, young girl.

175
00:11:39,346 --> 00:11:41,431
-Look at her always counting her chickens.
-[gasps]

176
00:11:41,556 --> 00:11:44,309
How can you do that?
I thought I was the one getting it.

177
00:11:44,434 --> 00:11:46,811
Give it to me
so that I can share with Namgung.

178
00:11:46,937 --> 00:11:50,106
Oh, God. Got three kids and for what, huh?

179
00:11:50,232 --> 00:11:52,817
Hoya is the only one
who cares about me these days.

180
00:11:52,943 --> 00:11:54,694
-[scoffs]
-[soft guitar music playing]

181
00:11:54,819 --> 00:11:57,572
[Suk-hee] He's the one changing
the window screens in the summer.

182
00:11:57,697 --> 00:12:01,868
In winter, he buys insulation covers
so the pipes don't freeze.

183
00:12:01,993 --> 00:12:06,039
He regularly cleans the AC
and checks the boiler.

184
00:12:06,164 --> 00:12:10,877
Even when the rooftop paint peeled off,
Hoya painted it as soon as he heard.

185
00:12:11,002 --> 00:12:15,674
He even came last week and installed
new anti-slip tape on the stairs.

186
00:12:16,341 --> 00:12:17,842
Didn't he do that last year?

187
00:12:17,968 --> 00:12:19,803
He comes every year to do it.

188
00:12:19,928 --> 00:12:23,014
My son replaces it
even if I tell him they're still fine.

189
00:12:23,848 --> 00:12:26,017
[chuckles] He's so sweet.

190
00:12:26,142 --> 00:12:31,064
Whenever Hoya changes the old tape,
it feels like winter is finally here.

191
00:12:35,652 --> 00:12:36,778
Hey.

192
00:12:38,321 --> 00:12:40,198
You should talk to Hoya about this.

193
00:12:41,283 --> 00:12:43,535
You're getting married.
You should ask him to…

194
00:12:45,996 --> 00:12:48,039
Don't mention this to Namgung, all right?

195
00:12:48,164 --> 00:12:51,167
You've got fire in your eyes.
So much anger.

196
00:12:57,382 --> 00:12:58,883
We're Namgung's family.

197
00:13:00,010 --> 00:13:03,597
You and me, Lee Yeong-do…

198
00:13:05,098 --> 00:13:07,976
Lee Sang-su. He has nobody else.

199
00:13:09,352 --> 00:13:10,854
He has no one but us.

200
00:13:13,565 --> 00:13:15,984
If I die,
Namgung gets this place. [groans]

201
00:13:17,652 --> 00:13:18,820
[sighs]

202
00:13:18,945 --> 00:13:20,322
[music concludes]

203
00:13:24,034 --> 00:13:25,201
[Mi-do grunts softly]

204
00:13:26,995 --> 00:13:29,122
What? When did you get here?

205
00:13:29,664 --> 00:13:30,665
Just now.

206
00:13:32,334 --> 00:13:33,543
You kept tossing around.

207
00:13:33,668 --> 00:13:37,714
Hmm. I took a nap earlier.
I think that's why.

208
00:13:40,133 --> 00:13:41,092
Hey, Mi-do.

209
00:13:43,762 --> 00:13:48,183
I know you like being alone
on your dad's anniversary,

210
00:13:48,308 --> 00:13:49,893
so I've always given you space.

211
00:13:50,685 --> 00:13:52,437
But let me stay tonight.

212
00:13:55,315 --> 00:13:57,525
-Would you?
-[sighs]

213
00:13:58,401 --> 00:14:01,821
All right, you can stay with me.

214
00:14:06,159 --> 00:14:07,160
Hmm?

215
00:14:14,334 --> 00:14:15,585
[both exhale]

216
00:14:17,253 --> 00:14:19,506
[hiccups, sighs]

217
00:14:21,424 --> 00:14:23,468
Should we go see a doctor?

218
00:14:23,593 --> 00:14:26,805
[groans softly] If it doesn't go away
by the weekend, I'll go.

219
00:14:26,930 --> 00:14:30,558
-Do you promise?
-Mm. [sighs]

220
00:14:39,901 --> 00:14:40,944
Namgung.

221
00:14:43,363 --> 00:14:45,824
I really want to feel butterflies for you.

222
00:14:50,203 --> 00:14:53,540
And I really want you
to feel them for me too.

223
00:14:55,792 --> 00:15:01,673
[gentle guitar music playing]

224
00:15:19,816 --> 00:15:22,235
[both smooch]

225
00:15:28,616 --> 00:15:29,784
[inhales sharply]

226
00:15:39,169 --> 00:15:43,923
[cell phone vibrating]

227
00:15:44,048 --> 00:15:46,551
-Is that from work?
-I don't care, ignore it.

228
00:15:46,676 --> 00:15:49,012
-[cell phone continues vibrating]
-[both smooch]

229
00:15:49,137 --> 00:15:51,222
-[grunts softly]
-Just answer it, it's bothering me.

230
00:15:51,347 --> 00:15:52,474
No, I don't care.

231
00:15:52,599 --> 00:15:55,018
-[cell phone continues vibrating]
-[breathes deeply]

232
00:15:55,143 --> 00:15:56,269
[sighs]

233
00:15:57,479 --> 00:15:59,063
-Fine, give me a sec.
-Mm.

234
00:15:59,189 --> 00:16:03,067
[cell phone continues vibrating]

235
00:16:03,193 --> 00:16:04,360
[Mi-do sighs]

236
00:16:07,739 --> 00:16:08,990
[Namgung] Good evening, sir.

237
00:16:11,367 --> 00:16:13,244
I'll call them
and get back to you immediately.

238
00:16:13,369 --> 00:16:15,747
-[sighs]
-Yes.

239
00:16:16,873 --> 00:16:18,625
-[line disconnects]
-I'm sorry.

240
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:19,751
Mm.

241
00:16:22,712 --> 00:16:24,339
-[line rings, connects]
-[Namgung] Sang-hun,

242
00:16:24,464 --> 00:16:25,882
at La Vita's local factory,

243
00:16:26,007 --> 00:16:29,177
they recalled everything
due to high aflatoxin levels.

244
00:16:29,302 --> 00:16:32,555
I'll call their headquarters,
you check on things there.

245
00:16:32,680 --> 00:16:34,641
-Yeah. ASAP.
-[music concludes]

246
00:16:34,766 --> 00:16:36,643
HUNMIN CONFECTIONARY

247
00:16:38,102 --> 00:16:40,980
It won't be easy, but since La Vita
wants to meet personally,

248
00:16:41,105 --> 00:16:42,190
I'll report back after.

249
00:16:42,315 --> 00:16:44,734
-Right. Talk to them and be flexible.
-Yeah.

250
00:16:47,779 --> 00:16:48,822
[sighs]

251
00:16:57,038 --> 00:16:57,872
MIDORI

252
00:16:57,997 --> 00:17:00,667
[Namgung]  Are you awake?
Work is being sorted out.

253
00:17:00,792 --> 00:17:02,168
Texting so you don't worry.

254
00:17:07,215 --> 00:17:09,843
We should go on a trip together
when things calm down.

255
00:17:10,426 --> 00:17:11,719
I know you love Taipei.

256
00:17:12,303 --> 00:17:14,973
Or maybe Hawaii?
It'd be kind of cool, don't you think?

257
00:17:16,808 --> 00:17:19,894
[computer mouse clicking]

258
00:17:21,354 --> 00:17:22,856
Oh, wow.

259
00:17:23,731 --> 00:17:25,567
I thought you'd come after lunch.

260
00:17:27,443 --> 00:17:30,154
Everyone, this is Park Su-a
from Snack Team 4.

261
00:17:30,280 --> 00:17:33,491
She's been assigned to our team today.
We'll be working together.

262
00:17:33,616 --> 00:17:35,785
-Introduce yourself.
-I'm Park Su-a.

263
00:17:35,910 --> 00:17:38,288
Nice to meet you all.
I look forward to collaborating.

264
00:17:44,794 --> 00:17:47,964
I really thought I'd made myself clear
the last time we talked,

265
00:17:48,089 --> 00:17:50,300
but you're quite persistent, Su-a.

266
00:17:54,721 --> 00:17:58,850
Manager Seok Dong-hwan, Jeong Yeon-ho,
Manager Yoon Jae-mun,

267
00:17:58,975 --> 00:18:01,686
Manager Jeong Seok-ho, also Baek Seok-u.

268
00:18:02,854 --> 00:18:06,399
Not to mention Director Yoon,
and most of his executive personnel.

269
00:18:12,071 --> 00:18:16,117
TF Snack Team 3,
your fourth sample tasted different

270
00:18:16,242 --> 00:18:18,286
because you used imported sweet potatoes.

271
00:18:20,163 --> 00:18:21,289
A mistake, I guess.

272
00:18:22,957 --> 00:18:26,920
So from now on, they'll be extra careful
when planning samples.

273
00:18:27,045 --> 00:18:30,590
I mean, whatever date
they absolutely refuse to read to,

274
00:18:30,715 --> 00:18:33,635
that's probably the planned date
to do the switch.

275
00:18:35,261 --> 00:18:39,891
So, the only reason you wanted to talk
is 'cause you want my team's schedule.

276
00:18:42,185 --> 00:18:45,104
I'm asking to be there
when your sample's scheduled.

277
00:18:46,397 --> 00:18:48,900
I know I'm being selfish,
but you can do that much.

278
00:18:49,609 --> 00:18:50,902
Let me handle the rest.

279
00:18:52,236 --> 00:18:53,446
[inhales sharply]

280
00:18:54,322 --> 00:18:55,365
[sighs]

281
00:19:01,329 --> 00:19:03,414
Are you really not…

282
00:19:04,415 --> 00:19:05,917
[inhales deeply]

283
00:19:06,042 --> 00:19:10,713
[sighs] The more I look, the more
you resemble Executive Director Yoon.

284
00:19:10,838 --> 00:19:15,218
-Huh? Wow. That frown is all your father.
-[quirky instrumental music playing]

285
00:19:15,343 --> 00:19:16,636
[squeak sound effect]

286
00:19:17,512 --> 00:19:20,223
[comedic slide whistle sound effect]

287
00:19:20,348 --> 00:19:23,810
Okay, I get it.
Let's pretend you're not related to him.

288
00:19:24,852 --> 00:19:26,396
I'd say you're prickly, that's all.

289
00:19:27,647 --> 00:19:29,857
Let's eat.
We gotta get back to work, right?

290
00:19:31,734 --> 00:19:33,778
It won't interfere with Team 3's work.

291
00:19:34,737 --> 00:19:38,992
Please, the day your manager schedules it,
just let me tag along.

292
00:19:40,034 --> 00:19:42,036
That's too dangerous. I don't think so.

293
00:19:42,662 --> 00:19:45,623
If a scandal like this breaks out,
the company will launch an investigation,

294
00:19:45,748 --> 00:19:49,794
and our new crop-related product releases
would come to a complete standstill.

295
00:19:49,919 --> 00:19:53,756
I'm not crazy enough to be part
of something that'll screw us over.

296
00:19:54,549 --> 00:19:55,591
Your food's getting cold.

297
00:19:57,760 --> 00:20:00,138
[slurping]

298
00:20:00,263 --> 00:20:02,056
-[music concludes]
-But if we release it

299
00:20:02,181 --> 00:20:04,392
under these conditions,
the quality will be inadequate!

300
00:20:04,517 --> 00:20:08,104
We can't get good results in the market.
I'm sure you know that too.

301
00:20:13,568 --> 00:20:14,736
Of course I know it.

302
00:20:15,695 --> 00:20:19,073
But you, Park Su-a, seem to be missing
what's really important.

303
00:20:20,575 --> 00:20:23,327
Our team won't be scheduling
any processes for a while.

304
00:20:25,204 --> 00:20:28,750
I heard that the peperoncino vendor
is having some issues too.

305
00:20:28,875 --> 00:20:29,709
What?

306
00:20:29,834 --> 00:20:32,462
I may look like a nice guy,

307
00:20:32,587 --> 00:20:35,590
but I have a terrible personality
and I'm basically a boomer.

308
00:20:35,715 --> 00:20:39,802
So, I get easily triggered
and I throw fits.

309
00:20:39,927 --> 00:20:41,304
[quirky instrumental music playing]

310
00:20:41,429 --> 00:20:44,640
The problem is that
I'm your direct supervisor as of today.

311
00:20:45,641 --> 00:20:48,019
Can you handle the power imbalance?

312
00:20:48,144 --> 00:20:49,687
[bell dinging sound effect]

313
00:20:52,231 --> 00:20:53,274
[sighs]

314
00:20:54,150 --> 00:20:58,196
-[gasps] Shit. I just can't-- Wait!
-[music concludes]

315
00:20:58,321 --> 00:21:00,198
JAEKANG LAW FIRM

316
00:21:00,364 --> 00:21:02,033
[pages rustling]

317
00:21:05,495 --> 00:21:06,746
[sighs heavily]

318
00:21:08,164 --> 00:21:09,373
[inhales deeply]

319
00:21:14,003 --> 00:21:17,173
-[combination lock wheels clicking]
-[latch clicks]

320
00:21:24,639 --> 00:21:29,769
[soft poignant music playing]

321
00:21:30,728 --> 00:21:32,939
[Seung-ho]
Those words hit hard back then,

322
00:21:33,064 --> 00:21:35,483
and I'd really like
to return the favor now.

323
00:21:35,608 --> 00:21:39,278
You're never going
to make your feature film debut.

324
00:21:40,655 --> 00:21:43,783
You've lost momentum.
You've lost your passion.

325
00:21:43,908 --> 00:21:46,869
That's why you're going
to fade into obscurity.

326
00:21:47,703 --> 00:21:50,790
And now… enjoy my film.

327
00:22:00,508 --> 00:22:01,592
[sniffles]

328
00:22:10,768 --> 00:22:13,604
-[sighs] Why are you following me around?
-[music concludes]

329
00:22:13,729 --> 00:22:14,939
I'm just worried.

330
00:22:18,526 --> 00:22:21,112
Wait, I must not tell lies.

331
00:22:21,237 --> 00:22:23,281
-'Cause I'm curious.
-Crazy.

332
00:22:25,199 --> 00:22:26,450
Hmm.

333
00:22:28,494 --> 00:22:30,246
That face gives you away.

334
00:22:31,664 --> 00:22:32,707
What do you mean?

335
00:22:33,374 --> 00:22:35,501
Don't clench your jaw so much. You're…

336
00:22:36,669 --> 00:22:38,629
embarrassed
and yet holding that emotion in.

337
00:22:38,754 --> 00:22:39,839
[sighs]

338
00:22:42,508 --> 00:22:44,844
You're in no position
to treat me like this.

339
00:22:44,969 --> 00:22:47,263
Just as you're in no position
to be releasing that picture.

340
00:22:48,931 --> 00:22:49,974
[chuckles softly]

341
00:22:51,601 --> 00:22:56,439
You see, you're acting like
you could win this with just one picture.

342
00:22:57,273 --> 00:22:58,608
But that leverage only works

343
00:22:58,733 --> 00:23:00,902
if you're willing
to deal with the outcome.

344
00:23:01,027 --> 00:23:04,780
Can you really deal with the outcome of…

345
00:23:05,948 --> 00:23:07,241
releasing it?

346
00:23:07,366 --> 00:23:09,076
You'll never know unless I do.

347
00:23:10,453 --> 00:23:16,417
I'm completely crazy as you can see.
So think twice before pushing your luck.

348
00:23:17,585 --> 00:23:21,339
-What would you do if I caused trouble?
-Then be my guest.

349
00:23:22,632 --> 00:23:25,384
What? Do you need permission to do it?

350
00:23:30,431 --> 00:23:31,557
[Mi-do sighs]

351
00:23:33,601 --> 00:23:36,562
[intriguing instrumental music playing]

352
00:23:40,650 --> 00:23:41,734
[grunts softly]

353
00:23:58,042 --> 00:23:59,043
[scoffs]

354
00:24:07,260 --> 00:24:08,219
[sighs]

355
00:24:09,762 --> 00:24:11,138
[music fades]

356
00:24:14,475 --> 00:24:15,476
SIM HAE-JU

357
00:24:16,227 --> 00:24:17,770
[line ringing]

358
00:24:17,895 --> 00:24:19,689
[Hae-ju]  Hey there, it's Sim Hae-ju.

359
00:24:19,814 --> 00:24:21,565
I run errands and do it all.

360
00:24:21,691 --> 00:24:22,817
Any updates on Mi-do?

361
00:24:22,942 --> 00:24:25,278
[Hae-ju]  Ah, the cloud server's
much harder to break into.

362
00:24:25,403 --> 00:24:28,030
It has two-factor authentication
and endpoint encryption.

363
00:24:28,155 --> 00:24:31,826
I just tried a brute-force attack
and, uh, got kicked out. It failed.

364
00:24:31,951 --> 00:24:33,077
Then what now?

365
00:24:33,202 --> 00:24:35,204
-[music resumes]
-[Hae-ju]  It's gonna take at least a day.

366
00:24:35,329 --> 00:24:37,915
Two days if you don't want
any logs left over.

367
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:41,127
But if it's saved on another cloud,
this is pointless too.

368
00:24:41,252 --> 00:24:44,463
Just meet with her and negotiate.
That might be faster.

369
00:24:44,588 --> 00:24:49,302
You think I haven't tried that, huh?
She won't listen to reason.

370
00:24:50,094 --> 00:24:53,264
-She's a nutcase.
-[Hae-ju]  Crazier than you?

371
00:24:53,389 --> 00:24:58,561
Hey, I'm a very reasonable person!
What are you saying? Okay, whatever.

372
00:24:59,353 --> 00:25:02,606
Blow the server up or the account.
Just fix the situation.

373
00:25:02,732 --> 00:25:04,483
Or you're gonna be the one
to blow to pieces, okay?

374
00:25:04,608 --> 00:25:06,610
[Hae-ju]  Hey!
I thought you were reasonable.

375
00:25:06,736 --> 00:25:08,029
[Tae-seung sighs]

376
00:25:09,113 --> 00:25:11,490
Ah, damn it. [inhales deeply]

377
00:25:12,575 --> 00:25:14,035
[music concludes]

378
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:17,913
-[heavy rain pouring]
-[thunder rumbling]

379
00:25:18,039 --> 00:25:21,876
[suspenseful music playing]

380
00:25:23,294 --> 00:25:25,880
-[lightning cracking]
-[thunder rumbling]

381
00:25:34,096 --> 00:25:35,514
[music rises]

382
00:25:35,639 --> 00:25:38,726
[rapid heavy footsteps approaching]

383
00:25:39,602 --> 00:25:40,644
[Yu-seong] What happened?

384
00:25:47,443 --> 00:25:50,446
-Sir?
-He's already dead.

385
00:25:51,697 --> 00:25:53,491
[gasps]

386
00:25:54,408 --> 00:25:55,618
It's not true.

387
00:25:56,827 --> 00:25:58,245
Tell me you didn't do it.

388
00:25:59,330 --> 00:26:00,331
Did you?

389
00:26:07,755 --> 00:26:11,384
[Chan-hui] It was an accident.
Get out of here for now.

390
00:26:11,967 --> 00:26:13,219
Don't forget the competition.

391
00:26:14,095 --> 00:26:15,304
No, sir. Please.

392
00:26:17,390 --> 00:26:20,810
-[lightning cracking]
-[thunder rumbling]

393
00:26:21,477 --> 00:26:22,478
Ko Yu-seong.

394
00:26:26,023 --> 00:26:27,900
Listen carefully to what I tell you.

395
00:26:28,776 --> 00:26:33,197
-[music builds dramatically]
-[thunder rumbling]

396
00:26:37,034 --> 00:26:38,994
-[lightning cracking]
-[thunder rumbling]

397
00:26:40,663 --> 00:26:42,623
-Hey, line?
-[music concludes]

398
00:26:42,748 --> 00:26:44,208
[inhales sharply]

399
00:26:44,333 --> 00:26:45,334
CHAN-HUI

400
00:26:45,459 --> 00:26:47,586
-[soft music playing over speakers]
-♪ It's time to start over again ♪

401
00:26:47,711 --> 00:26:49,755
[breathes deeply]

402
00:26:49,880 --> 00:26:51,674
♪ Look out for some… ♪

403
00:26:51,799 --> 00:26:52,967
[sighs]

404
00:26:53,092 --> 00:26:54,343
[man] Work on page 30.

405
00:26:54,844 --> 00:26:56,971
See? It's on page 20 here.

406
00:26:57,096 --> 00:26:59,515
-Uh, but rather than the topic on page 20…
-Yeah?

407
00:26:59,640 --> 00:27:03,686
…this one up here is more in line with
what I've been studying since last…

408
00:27:03,811 --> 00:27:06,063
[Mi-do]  Excitement didn't just fade
from my love life.

409
00:27:06,188 --> 00:27:07,398
[dreamy pop music playing]

410
00:27:07,523 --> 00:27:09,108
[Mi-do]  The realization suddenly hit me.

411
00:27:10,192 --> 00:27:14,029
I can't even remember the last time
my heart actually raced for something.

412
00:27:14,572 --> 00:27:16,323
When did I last feel a spark?

413
00:27:17,616 --> 00:27:21,120
-♪ When I need you someday ♪
-[sighs]

414
00:27:21,245 --> 00:27:25,416
♪ Will you stay the same? ♪

415
00:27:25,541 --> 00:27:29,253
[vocalist singing in Korean]

416
00:27:29,378 --> 00:27:31,589
♪ You're still my easy place ♪

417
00:27:31,714 --> 00:27:32,715
CHAN-HUI

418
00:27:33,424 --> 00:27:34,800
[sighs]

419
00:27:34,925 --> 00:27:38,721
-[vocalist singing in Korean]
-[arcade machine buttons clicking]

420
00:27:42,141 --> 00:27:45,519
[buttons clicking rapidly]

421
00:27:59,408 --> 00:28:02,536
[song continues]

422
00:28:02,661 --> 00:28:05,956
♪ Too fast ♪

423
00:28:06,081 --> 00:28:06,957
[sighs]

424
00:28:07,082 --> 00:28:12,296
♪ But I slow down near you
Till it all feels easy ♪

425
00:28:12,421 --> 00:28:18,093
♪ You make it easy but you don't know ♪

426
00:28:18,219 --> 00:28:25,100
♪ That's why I can finally breathe
'Cause of you ♪

427
00:28:26,185 --> 00:28:29,730
♪ When I need you someday ♪

428
00:28:29,855 --> 00:28:33,817
♪ Will you stay the same? ♪

429
00:28:33,943 --> 00:28:37,863
[vocalist singing in Korean]

430
00:28:37,988 --> 00:28:42,159
♪ You're still my easy place ♪

431
00:28:43,536 --> 00:28:45,955
♪ I still see you ♪

432
00:28:47,373 --> 00:28:53,087
♪ When I close my eyes
And lie in the silence… ♪

433
00:28:53,212 --> 00:28:58,008
[song continues playing indistinctly
over speakers]

434
00:28:58,133 --> 00:28:59,176
[chuckles nervously]

435
00:28:59,301 --> 00:29:02,805
Don't stare, all right?
This is awkward for me too.

436
00:29:05,015 --> 00:29:06,433
Forgot something?

437
00:29:06,559 --> 00:29:07,518
Hmm?

438
00:29:09,228 --> 00:29:10,896
-Like what?
-[scoffs]

439
00:29:11,814 --> 00:29:14,400
-[breathes deeply]
-[song concludes]

440
00:29:14,525 --> 00:29:16,986
-[quirky instrumental music playing]
-[gasps] Ah.

441
00:29:17,111 --> 00:29:20,155
-Mm. Bling Bling app is good.
-Bling Bling? Mm.

442
00:29:20,864 --> 00:29:24,159
-[cell phone camera clicking]
-[gasps]

443
00:29:24,285 --> 00:29:26,287
Hold it. You look so pretty.

444
00:29:26,412 --> 00:29:29,873
-[gasps] Mm.
-[cell phone camera clicking]

445
00:29:30,124 --> 00:29:32,543
Look left. Yeah. Sexy.

446
00:29:32,668 --> 00:29:33,961
[chuckles]

447
00:29:35,004 --> 00:29:36,046
[glasses clink]

448
00:29:43,178 --> 00:29:44,221
[exhales]

449
00:29:45,514 --> 00:29:48,976
It's nice to have a date with you.
I feel nostalgic.

450
00:29:51,312 --> 00:29:55,566
Listen, how about if we go on dates
like this at least once a year?

451
00:29:55,691 --> 00:29:58,861
What do you think?
It builds romantic tension, which is nice.

452
00:29:59,570 --> 00:30:01,614
-Four times.
-Hmm?

453
00:30:01,739 --> 00:30:05,034
Once is not enough.
It's better four times a year.

454
00:30:08,120 --> 00:30:09,538
What? No?

455
00:30:09,663 --> 00:30:13,584
[quirky instrumental music continues]

456
00:30:20,299 --> 00:30:21,884
[both smooching]

457
00:30:30,726 --> 00:30:32,269
[both pant]

458
00:30:34,104 --> 00:30:35,397
[both smooch]

459
00:30:39,652 --> 00:30:41,820
-[hiccups]
-[Namgung grunts]

460
00:30:43,030 --> 00:30:45,032
[rapid footsteps receding]

461
00:30:45,157 --> 00:30:46,909
[music concludes]

462
00:30:47,034 --> 00:30:48,494
[Mi-do gags]

463
00:30:49,203 --> 00:30:50,871
Hey, Mi-do. [grunts softly]

464
00:30:52,956 --> 00:30:56,126
[doctor] I reviewed your test results.
Your CT scan and X-rays came back normal.

465
00:30:56,251 --> 00:31:00,089
It seems to be indigestion.
How long has she been hiccupping?

466
00:31:00,673 --> 00:31:03,467
It's been about a week or so, I guess.

467
00:31:03,592 --> 00:31:05,928
-Right?
-Uh-huh. [hiccups]

468
00:31:06,053 --> 00:31:08,764
[doctor] Stress is often a trigger
for this kind of thing.

469
00:31:08,889 --> 00:31:11,934
If it doesn't stop by this week,
you'll need to come back to the ER.

470
00:31:12,059 --> 00:31:13,310
Okay. Thank you.

471
00:31:16,772 --> 00:31:17,773
[hiccups]

472
00:31:19,483 --> 00:31:20,776
[sighs heavily]

473
00:31:20,901 --> 00:31:21,819
YUSEONG UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

474
00:31:21,944 --> 00:31:25,197
You should get a health checkup.
Did you have one last year?

475
00:31:25,322 --> 00:31:27,783
Don't overreact.
Didn't you hear the doctor? [hiccups]

476
00:31:30,202 --> 00:31:33,205
Book it now. Okay, I'll do it.

477
00:31:33,330 --> 00:31:36,625
Uh, wait, wait a minute.
What do you think about this hospital?

478
00:31:37,710 --> 00:31:39,545
-[woman moaning sound effect]
-[smooching sound effect]

479
00:31:39,670 --> 00:31:42,423
-God!
-What? Is it bad?

480
00:31:42,548 --> 00:31:45,426
Is this a joke to you?
What the hell are you…

481
00:31:48,512 --> 00:31:52,015
What? Say it. What? Tell me. Huh?

482
00:31:52,141 --> 00:31:56,103
[sighs] Fine. Let's not argue.

483
00:31:56,729 --> 00:31:58,814
[scoffs] Really?

484
00:32:00,482 --> 00:32:01,442
[sighs]

485
00:32:11,577 --> 00:32:16,331
-[sighs]
-[playful instrumental music playing]

486
00:32:16,457 --> 00:32:18,625
You really brought that up
at the ER, love?

487
00:32:19,626 --> 00:32:21,628
But the hospital said
it wasn't a big deal, love. Hmm?

488
00:32:22,629 --> 00:32:25,007
And I think this is more important
for us, love.

489
00:32:25,132 --> 00:32:27,426
I just wish
we could do this naturally, love.

490
00:32:27,551 --> 00:32:30,888
We agreed to try, love.
You promised, love.

491
00:32:33,015 --> 00:32:34,057
Okay, love.

492
00:32:35,476 --> 00:32:38,437
-But get a checkup, love.
-Okay, I will, love.

493
00:32:43,859 --> 00:32:44,943
[grunts softly]

494
00:32:48,238 --> 00:32:51,283
-Do we have to keep doing this?
-It actually worked.

495
00:32:51,408 --> 00:32:53,869
Ending each sentence with "love" works.

496
00:32:53,994 --> 00:32:55,204
It forces us to act cute,

497
00:32:55,329 --> 00:32:57,414
-so it tones down the intensity.
-[groans softly]

498
00:32:59,792 --> 00:33:01,668
Anyway, you promised.

499
00:33:01,794 --> 00:33:03,879
-You'll have a checkup?
-Yeah, got it.

500
00:33:04,713 --> 00:33:06,173
[music concludes]

501
00:33:06,298 --> 00:33:09,259
By the way, your mom called me today.

502
00:33:09,843 --> 00:33:11,595
She said she's clearing out
the rooftop room.

503
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:13,347
She told us to take whatever we want.

504
00:33:13,472 --> 00:33:16,517
-Shall we go?
-Our rooftop? Really? Why?

505
00:33:17,851 --> 00:33:19,978
QUEENS HAIR SALON

506
00:33:20,521 --> 00:33:21,688
[cell phone chimes]

507
00:33:23,232 --> 00:33:26,026
Hey, Namgung.
I just got here a second ago.

508
00:33:26,944 --> 00:33:29,321
Yeah, I'll start cleaning it out.
There shouldn't be much.

509
00:33:30,197 --> 00:33:33,992
Yeah. Okay, call me
when you get off work. Mm-hmm.

510
00:33:40,040 --> 00:33:40,999
[sighs]

511
00:33:56,139 --> 00:33:57,140
Wow.

512
00:33:59,101 --> 00:34:02,521
-It feels like it's been an eternity.
-[gentle guitar music playing]

513
00:34:02,646 --> 00:34:04,147
[Mi-do]
I feel like we need something really big

514
00:34:04,273 --> 00:34:06,191
to happen the moment they walk in.

515
00:34:06,316 --> 00:34:08,777
But doing that would only end up
making the shoot even longer,

516
00:34:08,902 --> 00:34:10,654
and we'd need a lot more time
to prepare for it.

517
00:34:10,779 --> 00:34:13,115
-If you need it, you should do it.
-I should, right?

518
00:34:13,240 --> 00:34:15,367
-That's exactly what I thought. [chuckles]
-Taste this, Mi-do.

519
00:34:15,492 --> 00:34:16,785
Oh, oh, oh, oh, let me try.

520
00:34:16,910 --> 00:34:18,537
-[vocalist singing in Korean]
-[slurps]

521
00:34:18,662 --> 00:34:20,038
-Is it good?
-It's really good.

522
00:34:20,163 --> 00:34:21,748
-Is it? [slurps]
-Mm-hmm.

523
00:34:21,874 --> 00:34:24,167
Mm! Mm!

524
00:34:24,293 --> 00:34:26,378
-It's so late. See you later.
-[Namgung] Bye.

525
00:34:28,964 --> 00:34:30,382
-Oh, Mi-do.
-Yeah?

526
00:34:30,507 --> 00:34:32,426
-[Namgung] Here, take this.
-[gasps]

527
00:34:32,551 --> 00:34:34,720
-Good luck. Mm-hmm.
-[mumbling indistinctly]

528
00:34:37,973 --> 00:34:40,392
-Mm. Mm!
-[smooches]

529
00:34:41,059 --> 00:34:42,853
-Mm!
-See ya.

530
00:34:45,606 --> 00:34:49,985
What kind of performance…
[sighs] Never mind.

531
00:34:50,694 --> 00:34:52,237
Why do I keep…

532
00:34:52,905 --> 00:34:55,699
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

533
00:34:55,824 --> 00:34:57,034
-[kisses]
-[grunts softly]

534
00:34:57,159 --> 00:34:59,286
Don't do that.
I'm busy right now, honey.

535
00:34:59,411 --> 00:35:02,080
I should explain that.

536
00:35:02,956 --> 00:35:04,416
-[gasps]
-[kisses]

537
00:35:04,541 --> 00:35:07,085
Hey! Hey! Wait a second! [giggles]

538
00:35:07,210 --> 00:35:09,755
[echoing]  I said no! Stop it!  [giggles]

539
00:35:11,632 --> 00:35:13,967
[sighs] Hmm.

540
00:35:19,973 --> 00:35:22,225
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

541
00:35:28,482 --> 00:35:31,610
[water spraying]

542
00:35:31,735 --> 00:35:34,321
-[music concludes]
-[machine rumbling]

543
00:35:36,406 --> 00:35:39,368
[pants, grunts softly]

544
00:35:42,996 --> 00:35:44,039
[sighs]

545
00:35:46,416 --> 00:35:47,417
[scoffs]

546
00:35:48,710 --> 00:35:51,296
[sighs]

547
00:35:53,048 --> 00:35:55,550
Listen, this is bullying, you know?

548
00:35:57,302 --> 00:35:58,470
Bullying, really?

549
00:35:59,596 --> 00:36:02,099
Uh, the word is "exploitation."

550
00:36:04,142 --> 00:36:07,104
Two days ago,
I analyzed three years of survey data.

551
00:36:07,229 --> 00:36:09,940
Yesterday, I did a full run-through
of all peperoncino suppliers,

552
00:36:10,065 --> 00:36:12,859
and today, overtime for shipments.

553
00:36:14,236 --> 00:36:15,487
This is exploitation.

554
00:36:15,612 --> 00:36:18,657
Right, so Park Su-a catches
on fast, doesn't she?

555
00:36:18,782 --> 00:36:20,701
[scoffs]

556
00:36:20,826 --> 00:36:24,705
-So you admit this is wrong, don't you?
-I'm not happier than you, Su-a.

557
00:36:26,832 --> 00:36:30,794
But you're gonna keep…
focusing on your weird theories

558
00:36:31,920 --> 00:36:33,797
unless I give you tasks to distract you.

559
00:36:34,589 --> 00:36:36,633
[playful instrumental music playing]

560
00:36:36,758 --> 00:36:41,138
Two days ago, you were snooping around
raw material specs and guidelines.

561
00:36:42,556 --> 00:36:46,685
Unit price adjustments
and partner changes yesterday and today.

562
00:36:47,936 --> 00:36:52,441
You're checking if box lot numbers
and shipping labels can be rigged.

563
00:36:53,442 --> 00:36:55,485
And if so,
who inside the farm is helping out?

564
00:36:56,778 --> 00:36:58,363
Is that what you were looking for?

565
00:37:01,783 --> 00:37:04,411
I hate workplace exploitation too.
It's despicable.

566
00:37:04,536 --> 00:37:06,121
But what can I do?

567
00:37:06,747 --> 00:37:08,707
Your hero complex
is interfering with work,

568
00:37:08,832 --> 00:37:10,042
so I have no other choice.

569
00:37:10,167 --> 00:37:11,752
[music rises]

570
00:37:13,879 --> 00:37:17,966
I'm not asking for your help anymore.
And I won't cause any more trouble.

571
00:37:19,801 --> 00:37:20,844
But…

572
00:37:22,262 --> 00:37:24,890
how about you let me handle
the sample processing schedule?

573
00:37:26,475 --> 00:37:27,517
It's just that…

574
00:37:30,020 --> 00:37:33,940
I struggle with your ideas.

575
00:37:37,069 --> 00:37:38,278
Oh, my God!

576
00:37:40,113 --> 00:37:42,866
-Should I tell the vice president?
-[music concludes]

577
00:37:42,991 --> 00:37:45,160
I'm curious, are you trying
to get promoted?

578
00:37:45,285 --> 00:37:47,037
Are you aiming for director?

579
00:37:49,081 --> 00:37:51,166
What, do you think I have no ambition?

580
00:37:52,834 --> 00:37:56,088
Just don't let my ambitions
silence my conscience

581
00:37:56,213 --> 00:37:57,464
because of your actions.

582
00:37:58,548 --> 00:38:01,009
Don't let it get in the way of work.

583
00:38:04,596 --> 00:38:07,974
-Hey, where are you going?
-Playing hooky.

584
00:38:15,315 --> 00:38:16,441
[sighs]

585
00:38:17,984 --> 00:38:19,111
SWEET POTATO

586
00:38:19,236 --> 00:38:22,572
-[forklift truck beeping]
-[quirky piano music playing]

587
00:38:22,697 --> 00:38:23,615
[sniffs]

588
00:38:25,492 --> 00:38:28,662
Oh, my. My goodness.

589
00:38:28,787 --> 00:38:32,457
Did you… Did you do all this alone?

590
00:38:32,582 --> 00:38:35,335
Yeah. Uh, where's Namgung?

591
00:38:35,460 --> 00:38:36,628
I don't know.

592
00:38:37,212 --> 00:38:40,173
I guess he must be with my husband
at the senior center.

593
00:38:41,466 --> 00:38:42,676
And they're…

594
00:38:43,343 --> 00:38:46,888
playing. Solid gaming.
Game of cards. [grunts]

595
00:38:47,013 --> 00:38:50,475
Hate when he does that. [groans]
We're shorthanded as it is,

596
00:38:50,600 --> 00:38:51,852
but he's playing around.

597
00:38:51,977 --> 00:38:53,645
-Anyway, thank you so much.
-[chuckles awkwardly]

598
00:38:53,770 --> 00:38:57,607
Whoo! You're pretty,
but also a hard worker. Oh!

599
00:38:57,732 --> 00:39:00,193
Just look at all these.
You did a really good job.

600
00:39:00,318 --> 00:39:01,278
[chuckles]

601
00:39:02,112 --> 00:39:03,655
-[sword drawing sound effect]
-[music concludes]

602
00:39:03,780 --> 00:39:04,823
[Mi-do sighs]

603
00:39:05,323 --> 00:39:07,492
[inhales, hums softly]

604
00:39:07,617 --> 00:39:11,454
Hmm,  Slam Dunk,  where is it?

605
00:39:11,580 --> 00:39:13,331
[inhales sharply]

606
00:39:13,748 --> 00:39:15,417
Where is…

607
00:39:15,959 --> 00:39:17,669
[sighs] I can't find it.

608
00:39:20,255 --> 00:39:21,214
Huh?

609
00:39:25,260 --> 00:39:27,387
[grunts, sighs]

610
00:39:30,473 --> 00:39:31,600
[grunts]

611
00:39:33,768 --> 00:39:34,978
[cell phone vibrating]

612
00:39:35,103 --> 00:39:37,522
ALUMINUM CAN BASTARD

613
00:39:37,689 --> 00:39:39,733
That shitty lawyer.

614
00:39:40,108 --> 00:39:41,526
-[cell phone continues vibrating]
-[grunts]

615
00:39:41,651 --> 00:39:43,111
-[bookshelf creaks]
-Whoa!

616
00:39:44,112 --> 00:39:46,489
-[bookshelf crashes]
-[Mi-do groans]

617
00:39:46,615 --> 00:39:49,868
[train rumbling]

618
00:39:49,993 --> 00:39:56,666
-[poignant instrumental music playing]
-[groans, pants]

619
00:39:56,791 --> 00:40:03,381
[panting, grunting]

620
00:40:04,466 --> 00:40:07,219
[grunts]

621
00:40:08,220 --> 00:40:11,890
[pants]

622
00:40:12,015 --> 00:40:13,058
[groans]

623
00:40:13,183 --> 00:40:15,644
-[cord snaps]
-[yelps, gasps]

624
00:40:15,769 --> 00:40:21,358
[panting heavily]

625
00:40:21,483 --> 00:40:24,277
[ceiling light creaking]

626
00:40:24,402 --> 00:40:26,988
-[pants]
-[Tae-seung over phone]  Hello.

627
00:40:27,113 --> 00:40:29,532
-[continues panting]
-[Tae-seung]  Director?

628
00:40:29,658 --> 00:40:30,492
ALUMINUM CAN BASTARD

629
00:40:32,369 --> 00:40:33,411
[Tae-seung]  Ms. Lee.

630
00:40:33,536 --> 00:40:37,540
-[continues panting]
-[music concludes]

631
00:40:37,666 --> 00:40:39,376
[birds chirping]

632
00:40:41,002 --> 00:40:42,128
HOW TO STOP HICCUPS

633
00:40:42,254 --> 00:40:45,131
HICCUPS FOR OVER 3 DAYS.
SHOULD I SEE A DOCTOR?

634
00:40:46,383 --> 00:40:48,802
[cows mooing]

635
00:40:51,221 --> 00:40:54,140
[snores, smacks lips]

636
00:40:55,600 --> 00:40:56,559
[scoffs]

637
00:41:05,986 --> 00:41:07,654
[Su-a inhales deeply]

638
00:41:10,490 --> 00:41:11,658
[sighs]

639
00:41:15,829 --> 00:41:16,913
[gasps softly]

640
00:41:17,038 --> 00:41:19,749
Oh, my God. What?

641
00:41:20,709 --> 00:41:22,127
I'm worried.

642
00:41:24,629 --> 00:41:26,548
Right now on your head…

643
00:41:27,257 --> 00:41:29,718
there's a huge spider the size of my hand.

644
00:41:30,885 --> 00:41:32,345
-[gasps]
-No, no, stay still.

645
00:41:33,930 --> 00:41:36,933
-It could be a poisonous spider.
-Huh?

646
00:41:39,936 --> 00:41:41,771
In the army during training…

647
00:41:43,064 --> 00:41:45,734
my partner got bitten
by a poisonous spider.

648
00:41:45,859 --> 00:41:48,403
-Did he die?
-[scoffs]

649
00:41:48,528 --> 00:41:50,488
He didn't die, however…

650
00:41:50,613 --> 00:41:54,784
[inhales, groans] Do…
Do you have a tissue? I'll take it off.

651
00:41:57,329 --> 00:42:01,207
[soft instrumental music playing]

652
00:42:01,333 --> 00:42:04,544
[gasps] Are you crazy?
You said it could be poisonous.

653
00:42:07,380 --> 00:42:10,800
[chuckles softly]

654
00:42:12,510 --> 00:42:13,720
[scoffs]

655
00:42:13,845 --> 00:42:15,180
[clears throat]

656
00:42:15,305 --> 00:42:17,974
Jokes like this aren't funny.
Don't ever do it again.

657
00:42:18,600 --> 00:42:20,393
[chuckles softly]

658
00:42:20,518 --> 00:42:22,437
What are you waiting for? Kill it!

659
00:42:24,230 --> 00:42:25,648
Don't be so cruel with it.

660
00:42:27,317 --> 00:42:28,943
Spiders are great bugs.

661
00:42:33,114 --> 00:42:34,282
[sighs]

662
00:42:36,034 --> 00:42:40,246
It was able to survive
all the way until November.

663
00:42:40,372 --> 00:42:41,873
How could you kill…

664
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:45,543
such an impressive guy?

665
00:42:52,425 --> 00:42:54,552
[music concludes]

666
00:43:10,235 --> 00:43:11,403
[grunts]

667
00:43:12,612 --> 00:43:13,905
[door closes]

668
00:43:15,532 --> 00:43:17,575
[ceiling light creaking]

669
00:43:17,700 --> 00:43:18,827
[scoffs]

670
00:43:20,620 --> 00:43:22,372
-[electricity crackling]
-Oh.

671
00:43:23,832 --> 00:43:26,126
-[electricity crackles]
-[soft eerie musical sting]

672
00:43:33,967 --> 00:43:36,010
[sighs] Director.

673
00:43:37,429 --> 00:43:38,930
Are you happy to see me here?

674
00:43:39,055 --> 00:43:41,683
Cut the greetings. Move the bookshelf.

675
00:43:44,227 --> 00:43:46,563
[inhales deeply, sighs]

676
00:43:46,688 --> 00:43:47,856
Oh, but wait.

677
00:43:49,149 --> 00:43:53,403
If I help you to move it,
will you sign the settlement for me?

678
00:43:53,528 --> 00:43:54,529
[hiccups]

679
00:43:58,074 --> 00:44:00,743
And surrender the pic you saved
to the cloud account?

680
00:44:00,869 --> 00:44:01,870
What?

681
00:44:01,995 --> 00:44:06,040
So, no. Maybe it's better
if I just let you die here.

682
00:44:06,166 --> 00:44:09,502
[inhales deeply, sighs]

683
00:44:09,627 --> 00:44:12,672
[scoffs] Did you hear that?
I was thinking out loud.

684
00:44:12,797 --> 00:44:15,383
I've seen a surveillance camera
in the store.

685
00:44:15,508 --> 00:44:19,137
It caught you walking in here.
Plus, you were my last phone call.

686
00:44:22,807 --> 00:44:23,766
Hmm.

687
00:44:25,185 --> 00:44:27,854
-I really don't care.
-[intriguing instrumental music playing]

688
00:44:27,979 --> 00:44:30,482
I'll say that when I got here,
you were already dead.

689
00:44:31,357 --> 00:44:33,943
-[chuckles]
-Aluminum can shithead.

690
00:44:35,069 --> 00:44:38,406
Trash that won't decompose
for at least 200 years.

691
00:44:38,531 --> 00:44:41,367
[scoffs] I'm not planning
on living that long, so…

692
00:44:42,785 --> 00:44:43,953
Anyhow…

693
00:44:44,078 --> 00:44:45,205
[inhales sharply]

694
00:44:45,997 --> 00:44:48,124
…there's that. [exhales]

695
00:44:48,249 --> 00:44:50,627
And I'd say it'll last…

696
00:44:50,752 --> 00:44:53,213
-[electricity crackles]
-…another ten minutes before it falls.

697
00:44:53,713 --> 00:44:55,215
So you must decide soon.

698
00:44:57,967 --> 00:44:59,802
Just get lost. [sighs]

699
00:45:03,848 --> 00:45:05,517
-[Tae-seung] Won't you regret it?
-[scoffs softly]

700
00:45:07,602 --> 00:45:09,145
[music fades]

701
00:45:10,355 --> 00:45:14,400
-Okay. [sighs] I'll leave you to it.
-[music resumes]

702
00:45:17,487 --> 00:45:20,698
-Fucking nutcase. [sighs]
-[footsteps receding]

703
00:45:22,867 --> 00:45:25,828
-[breathes deeply]
-[door closes]

704
00:45:25,954 --> 00:45:28,665
-[sighs]
-[music concludes]

705
00:45:31,042 --> 00:45:33,628
Hey, you. Good job today.

706
00:45:33,753 --> 00:45:37,257
-Here. These are for you, young lady.
-Oh.

707
00:45:37,382 --> 00:45:39,509
-[chuckles]
-Thank you, ma'am.

708
00:45:46,015 --> 00:45:47,642
-Where's Namgung?
-Huh?

709
00:45:48,268 --> 00:45:51,646
Uh, he mentioned he had
to check the sorting station.

710
00:45:51,771 --> 00:45:53,565
Did Namgung give you a cut?

711
00:45:53,690 --> 00:45:56,067
He took everyone to the cleaners.
He's so smooth!

712
00:45:56,192 --> 00:45:59,070
[farm owner's wife]
Now we know where he actually was.

713
00:45:59,195 --> 00:46:01,948
Ah, so you were at the senior center too.

714
00:46:02,073 --> 00:46:05,326
[farm owner] Jeez, why would you bring up
the senior center?

715
00:46:05,451 --> 00:46:07,245
-[groans]
-Shut it. You're always there.

716
00:46:07,370 --> 00:46:09,956
It's all over your GPS history.
Don't you think I didn't know?

717
00:46:10,081 --> 00:46:12,584
-It's just senior, senior, senior.
-The GPS route.

718
00:46:15,670 --> 00:46:17,964
Uh… Oh, keep arguing.
It's all right.

719
00:46:18,089 --> 00:46:19,674
-Huh? What?
-Huh?

720
00:46:19,799 --> 00:46:21,551
[both continue arguing indistinctly]

721
00:46:21,676 --> 00:46:24,220
[Su-a]
If I check the transport driver's GPS,

722
00:46:24,345 --> 00:46:27,390
I might be able
to find out where the switch happens.

723
00:46:27,515 --> 00:46:29,601
[slow intriguing music playing]

724
00:46:29,726 --> 00:46:33,855
[farm owner's wife] Oh, hi, Mr. Oh.
You left the car running.

725
00:46:33,980 --> 00:46:37,650
We'll load all the goods on the truck.
Go ahead and rest in the break room.

726
00:46:37,775 --> 00:46:41,487
-You look exhausted.
-Yeah, thank you. Appreciate it.

727
00:46:42,655 --> 00:46:43,698
[sighs]

728
00:46:47,452 --> 00:46:51,164
-[cutlery clinking]
-[music fades]

729
00:46:51,289 --> 00:46:52,540
YANGJIN SWEET POTATO SORTING FACILITY

730
00:46:52,665 --> 00:46:56,210
-[funky intriguing music playing]
-[forklift truck beeping]

731
00:47:01,049 --> 00:47:04,719
[music intensifies]

732
00:47:10,558 --> 00:47:11,893
[gasps]

733
00:47:20,693 --> 00:47:22,236
RECENT ROUTES

734
00:47:34,749 --> 00:47:37,543
[tractor door opens, closes]

735
00:47:39,337 --> 00:47:42,840
[engine rumbling]

736
00:47:42,965 --> 00:47:45,385
[music concludes]

737
00:47:51,349 --> 00:47:54,143
[engine rumbling fades]

738
00:47:56,396 --> 00:47:59,399
[breathes deeply]

739
00:48:00,400 --> 00:48:01,567
[door opens]

740
00:48:03,236 --> 00:48:05,154
You must get told
that you're stubborn a lot.

741
00:48:06,364 --> 00:48:09,659
No, wait. [sighs]
They probably just say that you're crazy.

742
00:48:11,035 --> 00:48:12,120
[sighs]

743
00:48:14,163 --> 00:48:18,167
Just sign the settlement, Director.
It's better than dying, right?

744
00:48:23,256 --> 00:48:26,008
So what about your family?
What about your boyfriend?

745
00:48:27,468 --> 00:48:30,680
You just broke up with that guy
and are already back together with him.

746
00:48:32,014 --> 00:48:33,599
And now you're planning a wedding.

747
00:48:36,561 --> 00:48:41,065
-[Mi-do sobbing]
-[poignant instrumental music playing]

748
00:48:43,401 --> 00:48:44,652
You're crying?

749
00:48:44,777 --> 00:48:46,654
[sobbing]

750
00:48:50,908 --> 00:48:54,579
I figured it out a while ago.
You really love him, huh?

751
00:48:55,663 --> 00:48:58,624
[Mi-do] I think it would actually
be better for Namgung if I die first.

752
00:48:59,333 --> 00:49:02,336
I'm the main reason he sacrificed it all.

753
00:49:09,343 --> 00:49:10,928
That makes me even more curious.

754
00:49:11,763 --> 00:49:15,099
-[sobs]
-I'll ask once more. Here we go.

755
00:49:16,934 --> 00:49:18,227
Tell me you're gonna sign.

756
00:49:18,895 --> 00:49:23,357
[breathes deeply] Shit.

757
00:49:25,568 --> 00:49:30,698
[breathes deeply]

758
00:49:31,783 --> 00:49:34,368
[inhales deeply] Okay.

759
00:49:40,166 --> 00:49:41,667
You've earned this victory.

760
00:49:47,131 --> 00:49:48,216
[grunts softly]

761
00:49:49,217 --> 00:49:50,885
[grunts]

762
00:49:51,844 --> 00:49:53,971
-[electricity crackles]
-[cord snaps]

763
00:49:54,096 --> 00:49:56,265
[glass shatters]

764
00:49:56,390 --> 00:49:59,644
[pants]

765
00:49:59,769 --> 00:50:03,439
-[music rises]
-[continues panting]

766
00:50:07,610 --> 00:50:09,946
[gasps] You're bleeding.

767
00:50:10,071 --> 00:50:12,406
[pants]

768
00:50:23,209 --> 00:50:25,002
[music concludes]

769
00:50:27,588 --> 00:50:31,300
Won't you eat?
Traffic will be bad later, so eat now.

770
00:50:32,260 --> 00:50:34,679
[munches, slurps]

771
00:50:34,804 --> 00:50:36,472
Why were you there earlier?

772
00:50:37,181 --> 00:50:40,434
-You better answer.
-What are you talking about?

773
00:50:41,894 --> 00:50:44,146
-Are you hallucinating?
-[scoffs]

774
00:50:45,106 --> 00:50:46,148
[inhales deeply]

775
00:50:46,274 --> 00:50:48,776
-[slurps]
-You pretended you weren't involved.

776
00:50:48,901 --> 00:50:51,153
But you were playing detective
behind my back.

777
00:50:51,279 --> 00:50:53,406
-I've never done that.
-Oh.

778
00:50:54,156 --> 00:50:55,867
I guess you're still waffling.

779
00:50:59,203 --> 00:51:00,454
I guess I had you wrong.

780
00:51:01,414 --> 00:51:03,583
Listen, if I knew you played so safe,

781
00:51:03,708 --> 00:51:06,168
I never would have asked
a coward like you.

782
00:51:06,294 --> 00:51:07,253
So I'm sorry.

783
00:51:09,755 --> 00:51:11,007
[slurps]

784
00:51:12,091 --> 00:51:16,137
-[cutlery clinking]
-From now on, I'll handle this alone.

785
00:51:16,262 --> 00:51:17,513
So back off and stay out.

786
00:51:19,390 --> 00:51:21,684
-[cutlery clinking]
-Can you send me the picture?

787
00:51:24,145 --> 00:51:26,689
Okay. I get it.

788
00:51:27,690 --> 00:51:32,987
So now, I'll go and take one myself.
If I was a nuisance to you, I apologize.

789
00:51:34,989 --> 00:51:36,157
[Namgung] Just sit down.

790
00:51:38,117 --> 00:51:42,371
[soft instrumental music playing]

791
00:51:42,496 --> 00:51:44,832
I speak politely,
and you cross the line to scare me.

792
00:51:46,751 --> 00:51:47,752
For real?

793
00:51:49,045 --> 00:51:52,298
[scoffs] Seriously, this is unbelievable.

794
00:51:53,341 --> 00:51:55,134
-Hey.
-[sighs]

795
00:51:56,010 --> 00:51:59,555
Deok-sun, you've grown a lot.

796
00:52:04,852 --> 00:52:06,604
You're saying you don't like needles?

797
00:52:06,729 --> 00:52:07,647
SANGJIN UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

798
00:52:07,772 --> 00:52:10,316
-I have an underlying condition.
-What do you mean?

799
00:52:10,441 --> 00:52:13,235
Well, I'm scared of needles, so…

800
00:52:14,028 --> 00:52:16,948
Uh, they said
it's only like five stitches.

801
00:52:17,073 --> 00:52:19,158
It only hurts
while it gets numb, don't worry.

802
00:52:19,283 --> 00:52:23,371
I don't care if it's for one second,
stitches are not for me.

803
00:52:24,080 --> 00:52:26,123
[gasps, exhales]

804
00:52:26,248 --> 00:52:30,127
Just disinfect it and put a bandage on it,
and give me a week of antibiotics.

805
00:52:30,628 --> 00:52:33,673
Uh, the thing is,
if the wound doesn't heal properly,

806
00:52:33,798 --> 00:52:36,550
it could become necrotic or cause sepsis.

807
00:52:36,676 --> 00:52:39,178
I'm sorry,
but my advice is to get stitches.

808
00:52:39,303 --> 00:52:41,722
[music rises]

809
00:52:41,847 --> 00:52:43,599
Well, this one was even worse.

810
00:52:43,724 --> 00:52:46,560
But they just cleaned it
and gave me amoxicillin.

811
00:52:47,687 --> 00:52:50,564
-Please, let's just do that.
-[sighs]

812
00:53:08,457 --> 00:53:09,667
EMERGENCY ROOM

813
00:53:11,168 --> 00:53:13,337
-[music concludes]
-Do you think this will make me settle?

814
00:53:15,715 --> 00:53:17,383
I really doubt you will.

815
00:53:18,467 --> 00:53:20,678
You wouldn't even do it
to save your own life.

816
00:53:21,971 --> 00:53:25,391
-Then why won't you let them treat you?
-I hate needles, I told you.

817
00:53:25,516 --> 00:53:29,520
-I have a trauma with them.
-You expect me to… [hiccups]

818
00:53:29,645 --> 00:53:31,897
[sighs] …to believe all that?

819
00:53:35,943 --> 00:53:38,070
Ever had something shoved
under your nails?

820
00:53:39,071 --> 00:53:42,533
-I'm not sure what you mean.
-It's painful as hell.

821
00:53:43,617 --> 00:53:44,702
I grew up in an orphanage,

822
00:53:44,827 --> 00:53:47,580
and the director used to do that
to punish all of us.

823
00:53:47,705 --> 00:53:51,459
To avoid getting caught in audits,
he used an untraceable method.

824
00:53:52,251 --> 00:53:55,379
But more than the pain,
the waiting was the worst.

825
00:53:56,797 --> 00:53:58,966
Waiting for my turn was way scarier.

826
00:54:02,845 --> 00:54:05,473
[scoffs] Don't look at me like that.

827
00:54:06,474 --> 00:54:09,018
I turned out pretty well,
even growing up as an orphan.

828
00:54:09,935 --> 00:54:12,480
Pretty obvious. Don't you think?

829
00:54:17,443 --> 00:54:19,278
That's just bullshit, right?

830
00:54:23,157 --> 00:54:24,617
You almost bought it.

831
00:54:25,493 --> 00:54:29,080
-Hey, don't-- [sighs] This idiot.
-[cell phone vibrating]

832
00:54:29,997 --> 00:54:32,166
-Hello?
-[Namgung]  Where are you?

833
00:54:32,291 --> 00:54:34,418
What happened in here? Did you do this?

834
00:54:34,543 --> 00:54:37,004
-Are you hurt?
-Uh-uh, I didn't get hurt. [sighs]

835
00:54:37,129 --> 00:54:39,590
-The bookshelf fell, that's all.
-[sighs]

836
00:54:41,425 --> 00:54:43,761
Babe, I really gotta go, okay?

837
00:54:43,886 --> 00:54:45,638
-Hey-- Uh…
-[line disconnects]

838
00:54:50,559 --> 00:54:52,603
Bill the car repairs fee… [hiccups]

839
00:54:53,395 --> 00:54:55,606
…and today's hospital bill together.

840
00:54:56,857 --> 00:54:59,735
We can't meet
the settlement terms you requested.

841
00:54:59,860 --> 00:55:02,446
No studio in their right mind
would ever agree to that.

842
00:55:03,948 --> 00:55:08,869
Instead… I believe I have grounds
to negotiate for your return.

843
00:55:12,123 --> 00:55:15,209
At this moment, the studio has officially
appointed Director Kim Jung-man

844
00:55:15,334 --> 00:55:19,588
as your successor.
You know the guy. From college, right?

845
00:55:21,590 --> 00:55:24,301
I can dig into his past
and find dirt. Hmm.

846
00:55:25,052 --> 00:55:28,848
Heard he's got a gambling history.
I know a few entertainment reporters.

847
00:55:28,973 --> 00:55:32,434
Just tell me that you approve it,
and I'll get to work right away.

848
00:55:33,477 --> 00:55:35,896
No. Don't.

849
00:55:37,940 --> 00:55:38,899
Excuse me?

850
00:55:39,775 --> 00:55:41,068
[inhales deeply]

851
00:55:41,610 --> 00:55:44,196
-There's more to it, isn't there?
-What?

852
00:55:44,905 --> 00:55:47,825
[scoffs] I found it strange for a while.

853
00:55:48,576 --> 00:55:51,704
All you asked for
was double your directing fee.

854
00:55:51,829 --> 00:55:55,749
I mean, anyone would ask
to be reinstated as director.

855
00:55:56,625 --> 00:56:00,504
-But you, on the other hand…
-Because your methods are cheap and dirty.

856
00:56:01,297 --> 00:56:02,715
God, they're really sad.

857
00:56:02,840 --> 00:56:05,718
-[pensive instrumental music playing]
-Ah.

858
00:56:07,052 --> 00:56:08,220
Interesting.

859
00:56:09,722 --> 00:56:12,808
Director, can I give you
a crazy suggestion?

860
00:56:12,933 --> 00:56:14,560
No, don't bother.

861
00:56:14,685 --> 00:56:17,104
[scoffs] Keep holding out
and you'll break.

862
00:56:18,689 --> 00:56:20,316
So why hold out like this?

863
00:56:21,692 --> 00:56:25,988
I'm not only talking about the settlement.
What about what happened on that rooftop?

864
00:56:26,697 --> 00:56:30,743
Can't you compromise just once?
You seemed ready to die.

865
00:56:32,703 --> 00:56:35,873
[scoffs] Of course,
I looked into your background.

866
00:56:38,459 --> 00:56:40,127
It never ends well for you.

867
00:56:40,252 --> 00:56:42,588
[music rises]

868
00:56:42,713 --> 00:56:44,882
[Tae-seung] What's the point
of having all that talent?

869
00:56:45,799 --> 00:56:49,803
You have to learn when to compromise.
That's how you survive.

870
00:56:50,721 --> 00:56:54,266
Oh. Like you, I suppose?

871
00:56:56,435 --> 00:56:58,103
I looked into your background, too.

872
00:56:58,229 --> 00:57:00,064
You stick by Seo Ju-hyeok,

873
00:57:00,189 --> 00:57:03,192
and you're quite famous
for giving him absolutely everything.

874
00:57:03,317 --> 00:57:04,235
[scoffs]

875
00:57:04,360 --> 00:57:06,612
[Mi-do] From finding clients
to prepping trials.

876
00:57:06,737 --> 00:57:10,324
And if that wasn't enough,
you manage his personal life.

877
00:57:11,951 --> 00:57:14,286
You do whatever Seo Ju-hyeok tells you to.

878
00:57:15,371 --> 00:57:16,247
Is that so bad?

879
00:57:17,665 --> 00:57:20,918
I just sell my skills to the person
who values them the most.

880
00:57:21,752 --> 00:57:24,421
But I work myself sick every day
just to earn that.

881
00:57:25,506 --> 00:57:27,800
Don't you think doing that is really sad?

882
00:57:28,717 --> 00:57:32,179
-Kind of pathetic?
-How can anyone walk on only paved roads?

883
00:57:33,264 --> 00:57:34,556
You walk down enough rough roads,

884
00:57:34,682 --> 00:57:36,642
you step in a little mud now and then.
That's life.

885
00:57:36,767 --> 00:57:40,479
But Seo Ju-hyeok walks on paved roads,
thanks to you.

886
00:57:47,403 --> 00:57:48,779
Can I give you a crazy suggestion?

887
00:57:51,490 --> 00:57:53,284
Stop working for the highest bidder.

888
00:57:54,076 --> 00:57:56,161
Work for someone
who treats you like a person.

889
00:57:57,663 --> 00:58:00,749
You see, no one considers
their dog their peer at work.

890
00:58:02,960 --> 00:58:04,003
[scoffs]

891
00:58:06,130 --> 00:58:08,841
-A dog, really?
-You're right. Dog is not accurate.

892
00:58:09,925 --> 00:58:13,304
You're a son of a bitch
your owner could toss aside any day.

893
00:58:13,846 --> 00:58:16,432
[music softens]

894
00:58:19,059 --> 00:58:25,774
[scoffs, laughs]

895
00:58:26,817 --> 00:58:28,402
[inhales deeply, sighs]

896
00:58:29,903 --> 00:58:33,073
[sighs] You're truly funny.

897
00:58:39,204 --> 00:58:41,623
[pensive instrumental music continues]

898
00:58:41,749 --> 00:58:43,917
See if you can keep up the act.

899
00:58:57,431 --> 00:58:59,600
See if you can keep up the act.

900
00:59:05,397 --> 00:59:06,648
[whispers] I'm just joking.

901
00:59:07,941 --> 00:59:10,527
[laughs] Oh, did I scare you?

902
00:59:14,823 --> 00:59:17,284
It might be worth considering
a return to directing.

903
00:59:17,993 --> 00:59:20,454
I'm willing to do this
by any means necessary.

904
00:59:21,372 --> 00:59:24,041
But only if you want to. [chuckles]

905
00:59:24,166 --> 00:59:27,711
Fucking nutcase. [sighs]

906
00:59:31,799 --> 00:59:32,966
[gasps softly]

907
00:59:39,807 --> 00:59:40,849
[gasps]

908
00:59:44,019 --> 00:59:45,604
[sighs]

909
00:59:45,729 --> 00:59:47,564
[music concludes]

910
00:59:54,571 --> 00:59:59,701
Honestly, Park Deok-sun,
how is she exactly the same?

911
01:00:01,703 --> 01:00:05,082
-[scoffs]
-[keypad beeping]

912
01:00:07,918 --> 01:00:10,712
-Mi-do, you're home?
-Yeah.

913
01:00:12,548 --> 01:00:14,425
Tteokbokki  will be ready in a minute.

914
01:00:26,937 --> 01:00:29,064
[both chuckle softly]

915
01:00:32,234 --> 01:00:34,903
-[poignant piano music playing]
-[breathes deeply]

916
01:00:42,453 --> 01:00:44,204
[breathes shakily]

917
01:00:45,789 --> 01:00:46,999
Mi-do, what is it?

918
01:01:11,815 --> 01:01:14,735
Oh? Your hiccups are gone.

919
01:01:15,861 --> 01:01:17,779
No, they'll come back soon.

920
01:01:21,950 --> 01:01:23,494
No, they're really gone.

921
01:01:24,411 --> 01:01:27,706
-Huh?
-Nothing ever worked before.

922
01:01:27,831 --> 01:01:30,292
-What changed?
-Good question.

923
01:01:32,085 --> 01:01:33,629
They stopped for real.

924
01:01:34,254 --> 01:01:35,130
[cell phone vibrates]

925
01:01:35,255 --> 01:01:36,089
ALUMINUM CAN BASTARD

926
01:01:36,215 --> 01:01:37,132
[cell phone vibrates]

927
01:01:37,257 --> 01:01:38,091
PARK SU-A

928
01:01:45,599 --> 01:01:48,101
ALUMINUM CAN BASTARD

929
01:01:51,772 --> 01:01:54,274
PARK SU-A

930
01:01:54,441 --> 01:01:59,404
[dramatic rock music playing]

931
01:02:18,382 --> 01:02:19,466
THANK YOU TO KIM DA-HUIN, PARK SUNG-HOON,

932
01:02:19,591 --> 01:02:20,634
AND NAM DA-REUM
FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCE

933
01:02:20,759 --> 01:02:22,553
[vocalist singing in Korean]

934
01:02:23,136 --> 01:02:24,763
[Su-a]
I wanted the whole world to hate you.

935
01:02:24,888 --> 01:02:26,515
[sobbing]

936
01:02:26,640 --> 01:02:28,225
[Namgung]  Acting like
we don't even know each other?

937
01:02:28,350 --> 01:02:29,726
-Uh, yeah.
-Wait, "yeah"?

938
01:02:29,851 --> 01:02:31,061
ANY SPARE MONEY?
I NEED TWO MILLION WON MORE THIS MONTH.

939
01:02:31,186 --> 01:02:32,938
-[Tae-seung]  Go back to directing?
-[Mi-do]  Is that an option?

940
01:02:33,063 --> 01:02:35,232
-[Tae-seung]  Of course.
-Yes! Right?

941
01:02:35,357 --> 01:02:37,150
-[Namgung]  I don't think I can do it.
-Huh?

942
01:02:37,276 --> 01:02:39,111
[Namgung]  This is not a shonen manga,
you know?

943
01:02:39,236 --> 01:02:42,489
Please, just don't give up on your art.

944
01:02:42,614 --> 01:02:43,657
It really suits you.

945
01:02:43,782 --> 01:02:46,285
Threaten him again,
and I swear that I will kill you.

946
01:02:47,160 --> 01:02:50,414
I might just scare him too.
It'd be quite entertaining.

947
01:02:52,416 --> 01:02:55,919
-♪ Everything feels the same… ♪
-[music concludes]

